{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: the Git host choice design note, recut. Head 805534a0c564d8317db4cb7b585de443562c5747, branch planner/git-host-choice-20261027: one child commit on a9518f62, which I reviewed in 52a3660a. It merges cleanly onto the current Main aecabde1. Review request ded4d4fb (it replaces cdeece3e), checker promise 25ccdc05, request cc0bf648, planner promise ba77e1a2. Artifacts: notes (bd8727b6), the self-hosting note (3dd8884c) and the new note (ccca768b).\n\nRead order: the diff from a9518f62; then sections 4, 5, 9 and 10 in place, beside packages/contract/src/bounds.ts, result.ts and archive-binding-wire.ts.\n\nEach gap in 52a3660a is closed:\n1. Archive. Section 5 now says that without publication there is no journal archive: no scope archives, every entry stays in the scope's own storage, and the Room A archive passes do not run. It names the bounds that then limit a room, says what the members do at the bound (start a new room, or bind a host under section 8), and limits the \"keeps working\" list to a room within its bounds. The install screen states this beside the host choice.\n2. Deliveries. The refusal table gains the publish-file delivery from an application's act (the lending shelf, for example). It is answered at once with a refused result, no-repository, delivered back so that the sending act's outcome is final. A site-publication delivery gets the same answer. W1 adds one such delivery.\n3. Cohort tables. Section 9 names UNPUBLISHED_COHORT: register@21, directory@20, membership@8, rules@10, destination@16 and inbox@1. The new versions are each one above the highest today (register@20, directory@19, destination@15). Section 9 then lists every table that must hold the cohort: archive-binding-wire.ts (six cohorts today), CREATION_COHORTS, the R11 admission list, the CLI's CREATION_INSTALL_COHORTS with its pinning test, and PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS. K1's 76 is now tied to membership, rules and inbox being reused unchanged. Section 4 names the cohort, and under host none the install act admits only it.\n\nChecks: prose lines are at most 79 characters. check-notes bb23e50f..805534a0 reports 0 warnings, git diff --check is clean, and check-commit-messages reports 2 checked, 0 flagged.\n\nOne accuracy point for G2 or a later edit, not blocking. Section 5 says a scope at its bound \"refuses new entries with the bound's name as the reason\". The result reason is scope-full (result.ts:18), and the bound is named in its detail. Also, bounds.ts marks scopeBytes, scopeItems, scopeRecords and scopeRequests as \"whole-scope opt-in only\". For a scope that has not opted in to that capacity, the limit is scopeEntries (100,000 at or above the floor, plus kept entries) and then the cell's storage. Saying so would keep the operator's expectation exact.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One room shape with an optional repository, a named cohort with every table it must enter, and the archive and durability losses stated where the deployer decides.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The closed host list, refusal before signing for clone and read-token, and final answers to deliveries leave nothing pending and mint nothing for an absent repository.\n\nSimplification: good. One reason, no-repository, covers every repository path.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head 805534a0. Design note only; no gate is owed. The planner lands it.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bd8727b6ee598d8ce2bf3d99ffcb0b200c659559","binding":"assigned","head":"805534a0c564d8317db4cb7b585de443562c5747","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:25ccdc0588bc32754c78460e5dc2617b8f01bfef\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ba77e1a23804f950810e96272bd3cc2b7bc6b12f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:25ccdc0588bc32754c78460e5dc2617b8f01bfef","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approv